  "known_local_policies": [
    "Forbidden Flame preserves the complete original null-cost row; both full primary faces explicitly certify printed cost zero. Damage uses the actual original all-Mana consumption record and the original active CAST target allocation, not later current mana or a new target presence.",
    "Spontaneous Combustion uses the original latest closed own-turn submitted Elemental relation for both target enumeration and payload. Without it the spell is untargeted and deals random-enemy damage; with it an enemy character must be chosen. The enemy-only chosen domain remains an explicit local interpretation pending CN edge calibration.",
    "Rising Waves uses one original simultaneous minion batch, then the ordinary original-batch damage/poison death relation after its checkpoint. Only if that first batch caused no minion death does a second fresh-board batch execute; independent reaction deaths are not attributed to the first batch.",
    "Both waves remain one CAST/payment. Each ordinary wave uses shared current spell-bonus/routing/protection/death handling; empty initial boards do not invent targets or RNG. The exact secondary-reaction boundary remains a local policy.",
    "Version/hotfix alignment and CN rule-edge calibration remain deferred; no candidates are removed according to implementation coverage."
  ],
